# Not part of the image, and excluded so editing them does not rebuild it.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` into the builder, so every file in the context
# is an input to that layer: a one-line change to a release script invalidated
# it and forced a full pnpm build, for files the runtime stage never copies —
# it takes only package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, patches/ and build/.
#
# Kept out of the context rather than reordered in the Dockerfile because they
# are not build inputs at all. The build reads none of them; only test and
# release tooling does, and that runs on the host.
scripts
tests
features
.features-gen
docs
playwright.config.ts
vitest-setup*
